data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":2386,"item_id":"fc_096d8e18fe7ae64d016adb200694748191a8aa7860abb5f325","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"spec\\\":{\\\"format_version\\\":2,\\\"case_id\\\":\\\"wave-map-energy\\\",\\\"full_target\\\":\\\"Let n,m be positive integers; u:R^n×(0,∞)→R^m jointly smooth and q∈R^m have Euclidean norm one. Assume |u(x,r)|=1; for each (x,r) there is a∈R with u_tt−Δ_xu=a u; and on each compact interval J⊂(0,∞), u=q outside a compact C_J uniformly for r∈J. Define e(x,r)=|u_t|²+Σ_{j=1}^n|∂_{x_j}u|² and E(r)=∫_{R^n}e(x,r)dx, Lebesgue measure, Euclidean norms. Prove e(·,r) is Lebesgue integrable for each r>0, E is differentiable at every r>0, and E'(r)=0.\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"For every r>0, e(·,r) is Lebesgue integrable, E is differentiable at r, and E'(r)=0.\\\",\\\"parameters\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"n\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"positive integer\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"m\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"positive integer\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"u\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"jointly smooth map R^n×(0,∞)→R^m\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"q\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"unit vector in R^m\\\"}],\\\"hypotheses\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H001\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For all x∈R^n and r>0, |u(x,r)|=1.\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"frozen-target.md:7-10\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H002\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For all x∈R^n,r>0 there exists a∈R such that u_tt(x,r)-Δ_xu(x,r)=a u(x,r), with componentwise Δ_x.\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"frozen-target.md:11-13\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H003\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For each compact interval J⊂(0,∞), there is compact C_J⊂R^n such that u(x,r)=q for x∉C_J and r∈J.\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"frozen-target.md:14-16\\\"}],\\\"definitions\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"D001\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"e\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"R^n×(0,∞)→R\\\",\\\"definition\\\":\\\"e(x,r)=|u_t(x,r)|²+Σ_{j=1}^n|∂_{x_j}u(x,r)|²\\\",\\\"depends_on\\\":[],\\\"requires\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"x\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"R^n\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"r\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"(0,∞)\\\"}],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\",\\\"n\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"D002\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"E\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"(0,∞)→R\\\",\\\"definition\\\":\\\"E(r)=Lebesgue integral over R^n of e(x,r)\\\",\\\"depends_on\\\":[\\\"D001\\\"],\\\"requires\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"r\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"(0,∞)\\\"}],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"e\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"D003\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"Δ_x\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"operator on smooth R^m-valued maps\\\",\\\"definition\\\":\\\"Δ_xu=Σ_{j=1}^n∂²_{x_j}u, componentwise\\\",\\\"depends_on\\\":[],\\\"requires\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\",\\\"n\\\"]}],\\\"logic\\\":{\\\"classical\\\":true,\\\"rules\\\":[\\\"direct\\\",\\\"modus_ponens\\\",\\\"forall_introduction\\\",\\\"exists_elimination\\\",\\\"contradiction_classical\\\"],\\\"calculations\\\":[\\\"Finite Euclidean inner-product and finite-sum identities. All FTC, compactness, uniform continuity and iterated integration steps are justified in the argument, not assumed as calculation primitives.\\\"],\\\"primitives\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"R\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"real numbers\\\",\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"Real field with usual topology, order, and Lebesgue measure.\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"R^k\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"Euclidean space\\\",\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"Euclidean space with inner product and Lebesgue measure.\\\"}]},\\\"pins\\\":{\\\"lean_version\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"mathlib_commit\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"mathlib_root\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\"},\\\"inputs\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"frozen-target.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"placeholder\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"problem.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"placeholder\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"proof-draft.json\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"placeholder\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"source-context.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"placeholder\\\"}]},\\\"graph\\\":{\\\"format_version\\\":2,\\\"case_id\\\":\\\"wave-map-energy\\\",\\\"spec_sha256\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"propositions\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For all x∈R^n and r>0, |u(x,r)|=1.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H002\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For all x∈R^n,r>0 there exists a∈R such that u_tt(x,r)-Δ_xu(x,r)=a u(x,r), with componentwise Δ_x.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[\\\"D003\\\"],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\",\\\"Δ_x\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H003\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For each compact interval J⊂(0,∞), there is compact C_J⊂R^n such that u(x,r)=q for x∉C_J and r∈J.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\",\\\"q\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"P\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"target\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For every r>0, e(·,r) is Lebesgue integrable, E is differentiable at r, and E'(r)=0.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[\\\"D001\\\",\\\"D002\\\",\\\"D003\\\"],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"e\\\",\\\"E\\\",\\\"u\\\"]}],\\\"inferences\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H002\\\",\\\"H003\\\"],\\\"output\\\":\\\"P\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[\\\"D001\\\",\\\"D002\\\",\\\"D003\\\"],\\\"rules\\\":[\\\"direct\\\",\\\"forall_introduction\\\"],\\\"locals\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"r0\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"positive real number\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R001/argument\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S004\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"arbitrary\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Fix arbitrary r0>0.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"J\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"compact interval in (0,∞) with r0 in its interior\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R001/argument\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S002\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S004\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"witness\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Choose J using the earlier existence fact F001.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[\\\"F001\\\"],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"r0\\\"]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"C_J\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"compact subset of R^n\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R001/argument\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S002\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S004\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"witness\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Choose the compact set supplied by H003 for J.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[\\\"H003\\\"],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"J\\\"]}],\\\"argument\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Fix arbitrary r0>0. Choose δ with 0<δ<r0 and set J=[r0−δ,r0+δ]; hence a compact interval J⊂(0,∞) with r0 in its interior exists. Record this existence before choosing J as F001.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"r0\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"F001\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"There exists a compact interval J⊂(0,∞) with r0 in its interior.\\\",\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"r0\\\"],\\\"assumptions\\\":[]}],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S002\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Choose J by F001 and apply H003 to obtain compact C_J with u=q outside C_J at every time in J. For x outside C_J, u is constant on a spatial neighborhood, and constant in time on J; its spatial and time first derivatives vanish in the interior time interval. By continuity they vanish on boundary points as well. Thus e(·,s) is continuous, zero outside C_J and bounded on C_J for each s∈J, hence Lebesgue integrable. The compact C_J has finite Lebesgue measure. Since e_s is continuous on C_J×J, it is uniformly continuous there. For small h with r0+h∈J, FTC gives [e(x,r0+h)−e(x,r0)]/h=∫_0^1 e_s(x,r0+θh)dθ. Uniform continuity makes these quotients converge uniformly on C_J to e_s(x,r0), and finite measure implies convergence of their integrals. Since E(s)=∫_{C_J}e(x,s)dx, E'(r0)=∫_{C_J}e_s(x,r0)dx. Differentiating the finite sum yields e_s=2u_t·u_tt+2Σ_j u_j·∂_j u_t, where u_j=∂_j u.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H003\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[\\\"F001\\\"],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"J\\\",\\\"C_J\\\",\\\"u\\\",\\\"q\\\",\\\"e\\\",\\\"E\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S003\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"For each j, f_j(x)=u_t(x,r0)·u_j(x,r0) is smooth and compactly supported. Its derivative is (∂_j u_t)·u_j+u_t·u_jj, continuous with compact support and therefore absolutely integrable. Integrate first in x_j on a finite interval containing the support: the one-dimensional FTC gives zero because f_j vanishes at both endpoints. Fubini applies to this continuous compactly supported derivative, so its integral over R^n is zero. Thus ∫(∂_j u_t)·u_j=−∫u_t·u_jj. Summing yields E'(r0)=2∫u_t·(u_tt−Δ_xu). Differentiating |u|²=1 in time gives u·u_t=0. H002 gives u_tt−Δ_xu=a u pointwise, so u_t·(u_tt−Δ_xu)=0. Therefore E'(r0)=0.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H002\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\",\\\"u_t\\\",\\\"u_j\\\",\\\"u_jj\\\",\\\"Δ_x\\\",\\\"a\\\",\\\"E\\\",\\\"n\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S004\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"As r0>0 was arbitrary, the conclusions hold for every positive time; no endpoint assertion is used.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"r0\\\",\\\"e\\\",\\\"E\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]}],\\\"applications\\\":[]}]}}\"}"}

